From: thor <thor@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: thor: the ADSP sensor hub for FastRPC

PB-OS's qcs8550-ayn-thor.append (project-barry/pb-os 8ea4653): sensors-PD
restart tracking and the stock process types of the FastRPC context
banks, for the motion sensors (with pbos-0560). Tested on a Thor by
PB-OS (faff51e). The remote heap PB-OS's file also adds (its
reserved-memory node, memory-region and qcom,vmids) is in Armada's
SoC device trees since their 0623, so it is left out here.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
@@ -489,3 +489,41 @@
 	/delete-property/ qcom,use-erm;
 	qcom,vmax-mv = <1300>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * Motion sensors (SH5001 accelerometer and gyroscope) through the ADSP's
+ * sensor hub: sensors-PD restart tracking, and the process type of each
+ * FastRPC context bank as on the stock Thor, so hexagonrpcd's SensorsPD
+ * and RootPD listeners get the banks the stock ADSP expects (patch 0560).
+ * The remote heap, its memory-region and qcom,vmids are sm8550.dtsi's
+ * and qcs8550.dtsi's (Armada's 0623). From MaSi's SteamOS-ARM-SM8550
+ * (qcs8550-ayn-gyro-fastrpc / -thor-gyro-fastrpc-pd).
+ */
+&remoteproc_adsp {
+	glink-edge {
+		fastrpc {
+			qcom,fastrpc-adsp-sensors-pdr;
+
+			compute-cb@3 {
+				qcom,pd-type = <1>;
+			};
+
+			compute-cb@4 {
+				qcom,pd-type = <2>;
+			};
+
+			compute-cb@5 {
+				qcom,nsessions = <8>;
+				qcom,pd-type = <3>;
+			};
+
+			compute-cb@6 {
+				qcom,pd-type = <7>;
+			};
+
+			compute-cb@7 {
+				qcom,pd-type = <7>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
